L174: [25] McVittie, G. C. 1974, QJRAS, 15(1), 246–263, Distance and large redshifts, “...conclusions derived from the assertion that this or that object is ‘moving with the speed of light’ relative to an observer must be treated with caution. They have meaning only if the distance and time used are first carefully defined and it is also demonstrated that the velocity so achieved has physical significance.”
